    "campaign": "SUMMER",
    "caption": "Birria Tacos have been all the craze — and for good reason! This trend has taken the world by storm, and it has found itself in other renditions such as ramen.\nThis recipe makes use of a handful of chilies, as well as Libby’s Corned Beef. The texture of the corned beef goes great with this dish, and in terms of flavor, it gives off a nice, briny touch. Great for get-togethers and weekend dinners, find all the ingredients you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace!\nServing Time: 45 minutes\nYield: 10 tacos\n\nIngredients\nFor Birria Chili Paste:\n2 Guajillo dried chilis, deseeded\n1 Ancho dried chili, deseeded\n5 Arbol dried chilis, deseeded\n1 white onion, quartered \n5 cloves garlic, peeled\n1 beef bouillon cube\n1/2 tsp. oregano powder\n1/2 tsp. cumin powder\n1/8 tsp. cinnamon powder \nFor Filling & Assembly:\n\n1/4 cup annatto oil\n2 cans Libby's Corned Beef\n5 cloves garlic, minced\n2 1/2 cups water \nSalt to taste \n3 pcs. calamansi, juiced \n10 small tortillas \n1 cup colby jack cheese, shredded\n3 white onions, diced \n1 cup cilantro, chopped \n4 pcs. red radish, diced \nProcedure\n1. In a small saucepan, cover Guajillo, Ancho and Arbol dried chilis with just enough water to submerge them. Boil for 15 minutes, or until dried chilis are softened.\n2. Transfer to a blender, along with the remaining Birria chili paste ingredients and 1/2 cup of the boiling liquid. Blend until smooth.\n3. Fry Libby's Corned Beef in annato oil. Add garlic, and sauté until aromatic. Mix in 1 cup of the Birria chili paste, and toast for 2-3 minutes. Add water, then bring to a simmer. Season with salt to taste.\n4. Strain to separate the corned beef from the broth. Mix in calamansi juice into the broth.\n5. Briefly dip tortillas into the top part of the broth, or where the grease floats. Fry on a skillet over medium heat. Top with colby jack cheese, corned beef, onions, cilantro, then more cheese. Carefully fold in half and press to secure. Flip to toast the other side. Repeat for remaining components.\n6. Top each serving of Birria broth with onions, cilantro and red radish. Serve this alongside the Birria tacos for dipping.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
